<title>INDONESIA: GE Capital says buys 7 pct stake in Bank Bira.</title>
<headline>GE Capital says buys 7 pct stake in Bank Bira.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>GE Capital, a subsidiary of the U.S. General Electric Co, said on Thursday it had bought a seven percent equity stake in Indonesia's Bank Bira.</p>
<p>Mark Norbom, Indonesian country manager for GE Capital, made the announcement at a news conference held by Bank Bira in Jakarta.  </p>
<p>Parveen Gandhi, corporate financial advisor at Bank Bira, estimated 1996 net profit for the bank at 60 billion rupiah and forecast 1997 growth at 25 percent. Last year's net profit was 30.34 billion rupiah.</p>
</text>
